---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base title="Privacy" description="Privacy policy of pedalzombie.com">
  <article class="wrap prose">
    <h1>Privacy policy</h1>
    <p class="muted">Datenschutzerklärung according to the GDPR (DSGVO).</p>

    <h2>Controller</h2>
    <p>The person named in the <a href="/legal/">legal notice</a> is responsible for data processing on this site.</p>

    <h2>Hosting</h2>
    <p>
      This website is hosted by STRATO AG, Otto-Ostrowski-Straße 7, 10249 Berlin, Germany. When you visit a page, the
      server stores technically necessary access data (IP address, time, requested page, browser) in server log files.
      Legal basis: Art. 6 (1) (f) GDPR — legitimate interest in a secure and reliable operation of the website.
    </p>

    <h2>Local storage in your browser</h2>
    <p>
      The editors keep your presets, the selected MIDI channel, the MIDI device and your cookie choice in the local
      storage of your browser. This data never leaves your computer and is not transmitted to me. You can delete it at
      any time through your browser's site data settings.
    </p>

    <h2>Web MIDI</h2>
    <p>
      MIDI communication happens exclusively between your browser and your MIDI device. No MIDI data is sent to any
      server.
    </p>

    <h2>Google Analytics (only with your consent)</h2>
    <p>
      If you accept in the cookie banner, Google Analytics 4 by Google Ireland Limited, Gordon House, Barrow Street,
      Dublin 4, Ireland is loaded. It sets cookies and transmits usage data (pages visited, truncated IP address, device
      information) to Google, including to servers in the USA. Legal basis: your consent according to Art. 6 (1) (a)
      GDPR and § 25 (1) TDDDG. Without consent Google Analytics is not loaded. You can withdraw your consent at any time
      via “Cookie settings” in the footer.
    </p>
    <p>
      Google's privacy policy: <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" rel="noopener">policies.google.com/privacy</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>Your rights</h2>
    <p>
      You have the right to access, rectification, erasure, restriction of processing, data portability and objection,
      and the right to lodge a complaint with a data protection supervisory authority.
    </p>
  </article>
</Base>
